---
name: public_event
description: >
  One announced, public happening a resident could know about without anyone
  telling them privately (backend/cognition.py, attach_agents; issue #795).
  Built from a world YAML's validated `events:` entry and seeded as a t=0
  observation into every agent's memory EXCEPT the host's -- the host already
  carries it as their own commitment, at higher importance, from their
  schedule. This is what gives a model-authored day a shared anchor it can
  honestly plan around: #795 measured zero co-settled pair-steps under
  --plan llm precisely because nothing about the world was publicly knowable.
  Memory text, not a live model prompt.
inputs:
  label:
    type: string
    description: The happening, lowercase and article-led, e.g. "a guest lecture on gravitational waves".
  at:
    type: string
    description: The world location it happens at, e.g. "Irvine Auditorium".
  when:
    type: string
    description: Free prose timing, e.g. "this afternoon". Deliberately not clock-coupled.
  host:
    type: string
    description: The cast member holding it. Optional -- empty drops the clause.
sample:
  label: a guest lecture on gravitational waves
  at: Irvine Auditorium
  when: this afternoon
  host: Professor Tanaka
---
There's {{ label }} at {{ at }} {{ when }}{% if host %}, hosted by {{ host }}{% endif %}. It's open to anyone.
